# KPI Catalog governance

You are not only implementing features — you are designing the future analytics platform.

**SSOT:** `docs/engineering/KPI_CATALOG.md`

## Mandatory gate (before implementation)

Before finalizing any **schema**, **table**, **workflow**, or **UI** that introduces or changes a business entity:

1. Open `KPI_CATALOG.md` and check existing KPIs for the module.
2. Detect: new/improved KPIs, derived metrics, future dashboards, reports, audit needs, AI opportunities.
3. If the feature enables a new KPI or improves an existing one → **update the catalog first** (or in the same change set before claiming done).
4. Ensure required fields for those KPIs exist in the schema (do not ship UI that cannot feed the formula).

## Entry template (every KPI uses this exact shape)

```markdown
# KPI-NNN

Nom:
…

Module:
…

Description:
…

Formula:
…

Inputs:
- …

Required fields:
- …

Displayed:
- …

Status:
Planned | Partial | Implemented
```

Also document under each KPI or a linked section when relevant: **derived metrics**, **future dashboards**, **reports**, **audit**, **AI opportunities**.

## Hard rules

- Do not invent one-off KPI docs outside `KPI_CATALOG.md`.
- Do not skip derived metrics (e.g. efficiency %, variance hours, cost variance %).
- Prefer durable fields (`origin`, `consumption_status`, coded reference FKs) over free text for reportable KPIs.
- Status must stay honest: `Implemented` only when formula inputs are persisted and queryable.

```text
❌ BAD — ship plan-vs-actual columns with no catalog entry
✅ GOOD — add KPI-00x Plan Adherence % (+ derived efficiency/cost variance), list fields, then implement
```
